    // Use the repeating pattern "ababa..." (i.e., s[i] = 'a' if i even else 'b').
    // Then s[i] != s[i+2] because parity matches at distance 2, so chars would be equal
    // in a pure parity pattern; instead, we pick the pattern with period 2 and prove:
    // for any i, s[i] = s[i+2] would hold, which is bad. So we must use period 3 or more.
    //
    // Choose pattern "aab aab aab..." (period 3: [a, a, b]) which guarantees s[i] != s[i+2].
    // Check within one period:
